  "slug": "transformer-rna-84da",
  "summary": "Retrieval-augmented diffusion, ESM-IF embeddings, and contrastive learning are now being applied to protein inverse folding and structure database search.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is learned representations that connect protein sequence and structure. RadDiff pairs retrieval augmentation with a knowledge-aware denoising diffusion model for inverse folding, reporting up to 19% sequence recovery gains. mTM-align2 combines ESM-IF inverse-folding embeddings, 3D Zernike descriptors, and contrastive learning for fast protein structure database search. What is new is the pairing of generative diffusion with embedding-based retrieval and contrastive objectives. MELO-ED, a Siamese CNN learning locality-sensitive multi-embeddings, extends the embedding theme to approximating edit distance between DNA sequences rather than proteins, so it sits at the periphery of the shared thread. None of these works addresses conformational dynamics or ensembles directly.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-30"
}
